{"authored" [{"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int (x+7)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x-7\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{x}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+7x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.js