 "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-2x+C \\\\  & =2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7d97394870f1fe9e3f4b7ac54069df947f16f59e606861ad8963392c5a34fd5" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)+1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/state.json" "file_sha256" "8eb29a464f99641d7cbf45e34a94d59022209a3c9f400599ad18ced2c311c241" "basis" 1231 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033253/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-2429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-2429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(2\\sqrt{x})-\\int (2\\sqrt{x})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-4\\sqrt{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-2429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-2429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-2429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+6x\\sqrt{x}-4\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}-6\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4x\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-6x\\sqrt{x}-4\\sqrt{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-2429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-4\\sqrt{x}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot {x}^{2}-\\int {x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-2\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-{x}^{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C"] ["math" "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-14722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})-1)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-350960" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350960" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int (x+7)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x-7\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{x}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{6} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{6}\\,dx=\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}4{x}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{7})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{4({e}^{2})^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4(1)^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{7}]-\\frac{4}{7}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{14}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{7}-\\frac{4{x}^{7}}{49}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{14}}{7}-(\\frac{4{e}^{14}}{49}-\\frac{4}{49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{49}(56{e}^{14}-4{e}^{14}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{49}(13{e}^{14}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-350965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{52e^{14}+4}{49}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(3x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡(x))(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-12566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{2}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909a