and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\cdot (3{x}^{3})-\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-78963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78966" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(x){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e-x{|}_{1}^{e}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}(e-e+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{e}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-49712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,(x){|}_{1/2}^{e/2}-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{e}{2})\\,(\\frac{e}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\,(\\frac{1}{2})]-{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/2}^{e/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}e-\\frac{1}{2}e+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-350967" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-350967" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-2x+C \\\\  & =2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64f1a80fcbf9b958b44ca68cb901d19df13e72103da909ad0b579c8c4a7a81ba"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C"] ["math" "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] ["math" "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C"] ["math" "4x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)+1)+C"] ["math" "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "q-78973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/state.json" "file_sha256" "9c6cb8da2ff18b6632fc25ddba632188c622909939f22c9db62ce6bc71ce17a5"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038699/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d"}] "usage" {"q-78962" [] "q-78973" [] "e-3993" [] "q-114553" [] "e-494" [] "q-114579" [] "q-12568" [] "e-493" [] "q-12573" []} "basis" 1339 "retractions" [[17592186096976 :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx\\log_{2} (3x)dx$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186094263 17592186094264 17592186094265 17592186094266 17592186094267 17592186293944 17592186293945 17592186293946 17592186293947 17592186293948 17592186293951 17592186293952 17592186293953 17592186293954 17592186293955 17592186300057 17592186300058 17592186300059 17592186300060 17592186300061 17592186300085 17592186300086 17592186300087 17592186300088 17592186300089 17592186300106 17592186300107 17592186300108 17592186300109 17592186300110] "immutable_fields" [[17592186094262 :answer-field/correct] [17592186094262 :answer-field/id] [17592186094262 :answer-field/key] [17592186094262 :answer-field/type] [17592186293943 :answer-field/correct] [17592186293943 :answer-field/id] [17592186293943 :answer-field/key] [17592186293943 :answer-field/type] [17592186293950 :answer-field/correct] [17592186293950 :answer-field/id] [17592186293950 :answer-field/key] [17592186293950 :answer-field/type] [17592186300056 :answer-field/correct] [17592186300056 :answer-field/id] [17592186300056 :answer-field/key] [17592186300056 :answer-field/type] [17592186300084 :answer-field/correct] [17592186300084 :answer-field/id] [17592186300084 :answer-field/key] [17592186300084 :answer-field/type] [17592186300105 :answer-field/correct] [17592186300105 :answer-field/id] [17592186300105 :answer-field/key] [17592186300105 :a